---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const checker =
  import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CHECKER_ORIGIN || 'http://localhost:5173';
---

<Page
  article
  title="Instagram follow-back checker: preview & limitations"
  description="Upload Instagram JSON, HTML or ZIP relationship files to see non-followers immediately, with optional history and a separate automatic-integration preview."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">THE MUTUALLENS CHECKER</p><h1>
    Follow-back checking,<br />with the context intact.
  </h1><p class="lede">
    Upload your followers and following files. MutualLens immediately shows who
    appears in following but not followers, with search, profile links and
    complete exports.
  </p>
  <aside class="article-note">
    <strong>Preview status: automatic checks unavailable.</strong><p>
      The mandatory website-only automatic workflow has not passed its
      complete-list, approximately 6,000 × 6,000 live-account, and recurring
      zero-cash gates. The current product is a preview, not a finished
      automatic service.
    </p>
  </aside>
  <h2>What you can do now</h2><p>
    Explore a clearly labeled synthetic dataset with 6,000 records in each
    direction, or select supported Instagram JSON, HTML or ZIP relationship
    files for local comparison. Search the resulting lists, change categories,
    sort by username, and download CSV or JSON reports. You can explicitly save
    snapshots in this browser and compare compatible sources.
  </p><p>
    Upload comparison needs no username, date or confirmation checkbox. The
    separate automatic integration still has its own live-source and capacity
    gates.
  </p>
  <div class="article-actions">
    <a class="button primary" href={`${checker}/#import`}
      >Upload your Instagram files <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
    ><a href={`${checker}/#automatic`}>Automatic checking status</a>
  </div><p class="small muted">
    The automatic entry opens the checker’s honest unavailable state. No real
    request returns sample results.
  </p>
  <h2>What your uploaded report means</h2><p>
    Followers and following are compared as supplied. Mutuals appear in both;
    the primary non-followers category is following minus followers. Ordinary
    supported uploads are assumed complete for this mathematical comparison,
    without pretending they are independently verified on Instagram.
  </p><p>
    Known missing parts, skipped rows or conflicting identities qualify the
    usable results instead of hiding them all. Ambiguous identities are isolated
    from negative comparisons. A whole missing direction remains an error. A
    recognized empty list is valid.
  </p>
  <h2>No arbitrary account-size cutoff</h2><p>
    The comparison does not truncate lists at a follower or following count.
    Browser memory protections and source limits still matter. A safe resource
    failure should explain the limit and stop processing, not quietly return a
    smaller complete-looking report.
  </p>
  <h2>Privacy follows the workflow</h2><p>
    Imported files are processed on your device. Saving is off by default, and
    you can delete app-controlled local snapshots. A future automatic workflow
    would involve MutualLens’s backend and an acquisition provider processing
    the requested account data; it would not be entirely on-device.
  </p><p>
    The checker runs on a separate browser origin from these public pages and
    contains no advertising or marketing scripts. Read the <a href="/privacy/"
      >privacy draft</a
    > for storage and hosting limitations.
  </p>
  <h2>One report cannot explain intent</h2><p>
    An account absent from a supplied list may never have followed you, may have
    changed its username, or may reflect a source or timing difference. A
    current report does not prove a historical unfollow. <a
      href="/guides/not-following-back-vs-unfollowed/"
      >Learn how to interpret changes.</a
    >
  </p>
</Page>
